{% comment %}
  Renders where this product is in stock, in one of two shapes.

  MANY VARIANTS — a matrix. Locations run across the top, variants down the left,
  so a customer can pick a size *because* it is available rather than finding out
  after clicking Add to cart. Collapsed it shows a three-row window around the
  selected variant (one either side, or the nearest three at the ends), so the
  block stays about as tall as the list it replaced; a toggle reveals the rest.

  ONE VARIANT — a list, one row per location, status on the right. There is no
  size to compare, so a matrix would be a table with a single meaningless row.

  Status only in both — no quantities, no "last few" state.

  The locations shown, their order, their customer-facing labels and an optional
  note all come from the block's "Locations" setting, one per line:

      Recharge | Our stock | Ships today
      Partner Supply | Partner stock

  Field 1 is the location name exactly as it reads in Shopify admin (Settings →
  Locations). Field 2 is the label shown to the customer; omit it and the Shopify
  name is used. Field 3 is an optional second line — use it to say what that
  location means for delivery. It is free text and never inferred, so nothing is
  promised that the shop hasn't promised.

  Availability for each variant/location pair, first hit wins:

  1. METAFIELD — a JSON list on the variant, then the product. Namespace and key
     are configurable, defaulting to `custom.stock_by_location`. Each object is
     matched to a configured location by `name`, and read as in stock when
     `available` is true, or when `quantity` is above zero:

       [{ "name": "Recharge", "quantity": 4 },
        { "name": "Partner Supply", "quantity": 0 }]

     **This is the live source on this store.** A Shopify Flow writes it within
     seconds of any inventory change — see `scripts/flow-stock-by-location.md`
     for the trigger, the mutation, and its Liquid template.

  2. STORE AVAILABILITY — `variant.store_availabilities`, a fallback that needs
     no sync at all, but which Shopify populates only when a location has local
     pickup enabled. Pickup is deliberately off on this store — it would show
     customers a pickup option at checkout — so in practice this array is always
     empty here and source 1 does all the work. Left in place because it costs
     nothing and starts working by itself if pickup is ever turned on. Note that
     the matrix reads it once per variant, so switching pickup on turns this into
     N lookups per page; the metafield stays the fast path either way.

  The resolution loop is written out twice, once per shape. Liquid has no way to
  share it — `render` gets a fresh scope and can't hand a value back — and a
  captured string would be worse to read than the duplication.

  Every configured location is always shown, on every product, whether or not
  either source had anything to say about it. A location neither source resolves
  reads as out of stock — Shopify omits a location from `store_availabilities`
  entirely when it doesn't stock the variant, which for display purposes is the
  same thing. So there is no need to stock every product at every location.

  The consequence of always rendering: if the metafield is empty store-wide —
  the backfill never ran, or the Flow is switched off — every cell reads "out of
  stock" on every product. That is a deliberate trade, since the block is meant
  to be a fixed part of the page and a missing one would read as a bug. If the
  whole catalogue goes out of stock at once, check the Flow before suspecting
  the theme. The `debug` setting prints what actually arrived.

  The outer element's id is swapped by `assets/product-info.js`
  (`updateSourceFromDestination('StockLocations')`) on variant change — Dawn only
  refreshes a fixed list of ids, so renaming the id silently freezes this block
  on the first variant.

  Accepts:
    - product:    {Object} Product Liquid object
    - block:      {Object} Block object, for settings
    - section_id: {String} Section ID for unique element IDs

  Usage:
    {%- render 'product-stock-locations', product: product, block: block, section_id: section.id -%}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign selected_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign ns = block.settings.metafield_namespace | default: 'custom'
  assign mkey = block.settings.metafield_key | default: 'stock_by_location'

  assign product_entries = product.metafields[ns][mkey].value

  assign config_lines = block.settings.locations | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'

  comment
    The matrix only earns its keep when there is a real choice to make. A
    default-variant product would otherwise get a column headed "Default Title".
  endcomment
  assign show_variants = false
  unless product.has_only_default_variant
    if product.variants.size > 1
      assign show_variants = true
    endif
  endunless

  comment
    The left-hand column is headed by the option name when there is exactly one
    option ("Size"), and left blank otherwise — a matrix corner needs no label,
    and joined option names read as noise.
  endcomment
  assign variant_heading = ''
  if show_variants and product.options.size == 1
    assign variant_heading = product.options.first
  endif

  comment
    Neighbours are what a customer reaches for when their size is out, so the
    collapsed window answers "what else is close?" without expanding anything.
  endcomment
  assign variant_count = product.variants.size

  assign selected_index = 0
  for v in product.variants
    if v.id == selected_variant.id
      assign selected_index = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign window_start = selected_index | minus: 1
  if window_start < 0
    assign window_start = 0
  endif
  assign max_start = variant_count | minus: 3
  if max_start < 0
    assign max_start = 0
  endif
  if window_start > max_start
    assign window_start = max_start
  endif
  assign window_end = window_start | plus: 2

  assign show_toggle = false
  if show_variants and variant_count > 3
    assign show_toggle = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if config_lines.size > 0 -%}
  {{ 'component-stock-locations.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <div class="stock-locations" id="StockLocations-{{ section_id }}">
    <h3 class="stock-locations__title">
      {{- 'products.product.stock_locations.title' | t -}}
    </h3>

    {%- if show_variants -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        CSS-only disclosure, so the block keeps its no-JS promise. Known wart:
        product-info.js replaces this element's contents on variant change, so an
        expanded table collapses again when a different size is picked.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if show_toggle -%}
        <input type="checkbox" class="stock-toggle" id="StockAllSizes-{{ section_id }}">
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="stock-locations__scroll">
        <table class="stock-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="stock-table__corner">{{ variant_heading | escape }}</th>
              {%- for line in config_lines -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign parts = line | split: '|'
                  assign loc_name = parts[0] | strip
                  if loc_name == blank
                    continue
                  endif
                  assign loc_label = parts[1] | strip
                  if loc_label == blank
                    assign loc_label = loc_name
                  endif
                  assign loc_note = parts[2] | strip
                -%}
                <th scope="col" class="stock-table__location">
                  <span class="stock-table__location-name">{{ loc_label | escape }}</span>
                  {%- if loc_note != blank -%}
                    <span class="stock-table__location-note">{{ loc_note | escape }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </th>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </tr>
          </thead>

          <tbody>
            {%- for row_variant in product.variants -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign entries = row_variant.metafields[ns][mkey].value
                if entries == blank
                  assign entries = product_entries
                endif
                assign availabilities = row_variant.store_availabilities

                assign row_classes = 'stock-table__row'
                if row_variant.id == selected_variant.id
                  assign row_classes = row_classes | append: ' stock-table__row--selected'
                  assign is_selected = true
                else
                  assign is_selected = false
                endif
                if show_toggle
                  if forloop.index0 >= window_start and forloop.index0 <= window_end
                    assign row_classes = row_classes | append: ' stock-table__row--near'
                    if forloop.index0 == window_end
                      assign row_classes = row_classes | append: ' stock-table__row--near-last'
                    endif
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
              <tr class="{{ row_classes }}">
                <th scope="row" class="stock-table__variant">
                  {{- row_variant.title | escape -}}
                  {%- if is_selected -%}
                    <span class="visually-hidden">
                      ({{ 'products.product.stock_locations.selected' | t }})
                    </span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </th>

                {%- for line in config_lines -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign parts = line | split: '|'
                    assign loc_name = parts[0] | strip
                    if loc_name == blank
                      continue
                    endif
                    assign loc_key = loc_name | downcase

                    assign in_stock = false
                    assign found = false

                    for entry in entries
                      assign entry_key = entry.name | strip | downcase
                      if entry_key != loc_key
                        continue
                      endif
                      assign found = true
                      if entry.available == true or entry.available == false
                        assign in_stock = entry.available
                      else
                        assign entry_qty = entry.quantity | plus: 0
                        if entry_qty > 0
                          assign in_stock = true
                        endif
                      endif
                      break
                    endfor

                    unless found
                      for availability in availabilities
                        assign availability_key = availability.location.name | strip | downcase
                        if availability_key != loc_key
                          continue
                        endif
                        assign in_stock = availability.available
                        break
                      endfor
                    endunless

                    if in_stock
                      assign state = 'in'
                      assign state_label = 'products.product.stock_locations.in_stock' | t
                    else
                      assign state = 'out'
                      assign state_label = 'products.product.stock_locations.out_of_stock' | t
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <td class="stock-cell stock-cell--{{ state }}">
                    <span class="stock-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="stock-cell__label">{{ state_label }}</span>
                  </td>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {%- if show_toggle -%}
        <label class="stock-toggle__label" for="StockAllSizes-{{ section_id }}">
          <span class="stock-toggle__text stock-toggle__text--more">
            {{- 'products.product.stock_locations.show_all' | t -}}
          </span>
          <span class="stock-toggle__text stock-toggle__text--less">
            {{- 'products.product.stock_locations.show_less' | t -}}
          </span>
          <svg
            class="stock-toggle__caret"
            viewBox="0 0 12 8"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
            focusable="false"
          >
            <path d="M1 1.5 6 6.5l5-5" />
          </svg>
        </label>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Single variant — one row per location.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign entries = selected_variant.metafields[ns][mkey].value
        if entries == blank
          assign entries = product_entries
        endif
        assign availabilities = selected_variant.store_availabilities
      -%}
      <ul class="stock-locations__list" role="list">
        {%- for line in config_lines -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign parts = line | split: '|'
            assign loc_name = parts[0] | strip
            if loc_name == blank
              continue
            endif
            assign loc_key = loc_name | downcase
            assign loc_label = parts[1] | strip
            if loc_label == blank
              assign loc_label = loc_name
            endif
            assign loc_note = parts[2] | strip

            assign in_stock = false
            assign found = false

            for entry in entries
              assign entry_key = entry.name | strip | downcase
              if entry_key != loc_key
                continue
              endif
              assign found = true
              if entry.available == true or entry.available == false
                assign in_stock = entry.available
              else
                assign entry_qty = entry.quantity | plus: 0
                if entry_qty > 0
                  assign in_stock = true
                endif
              endif
              break
            endfor

            unless found
              for availability in availabilities
                assign availability_key = availability.location.name | strip | downcase
                if availability_key != loc_key
                  continue
                endif
                assign in_stock = availability.available
                break
              endfor
            endunless

            if in_stock
              assign state = 'in'
              assign state_label = 'products.product.stock_locations.in_stock' | t
            else
              assign state = 'out'
              assign state_label = 'products.product.stock_locations.out_of_stock' | t
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="stock-row stock-row--{{ state }}">
            <span class="stock-row__name">
              {{ loc_label | escape }}
              {%- if loc_note != blank -%}
                <span class="stock-row__note">{{ loc_note | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <span class="stock-row__status">
              <span class="stock-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ state_label }}
            </span>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Diagnostics. Off by default, and only ever switched on from the theme
      editor. Prints what Shopify handed the theme for the selected variant,
      which is the only way to tell an empty `store_availabilities` (local pickup
      off) apart from a location-name mismatch.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if block.settings.debug -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign debug_entries = selected_variant.metafields[ns][mkey].value
        if debug_entries == blank
          assign debug_entries = product_entries
        endif
        assign debug_availabilities = selected_variant.store_availabilities
      -%}
      <pre class="stock-locations__debug">
variant:                {{ selected_variant.title }} (id {{ selected_variant.id }})
variant.available:      {{ selected_variant.available }}
inventory_management:   {{ selected_variant.inventory_management | default: '(not tracked)' }}
inventory_quantity:     {{ selected_variant.inventory_quantity }}
variants on product:    {{ variant_count }} (matrix: {{ show_variants }}, toggle: {{ show_toggle }})
selected index:         {{ selected_index }} (window {{ window_start }}–{{ window_end }})
store_availabilities:   {{ debug_availabilities.size | default: 0 }} returned
{% for a in debug_availabilities %}  - name: "{{ a.location.name }}" | available: {{ a.available }} | pick_up_enabled: {{ a.pick_up_enabled }}
{% else %}  (none — local pickup is off on every location, or this variant is
   stocked at no location at all)
{% endfor %}metafield {{ ns }}.{{ mkey }}: {{ debug_entries.size | default: 0 }} entries
{% for e in debug_entries %}  - name: "{{ e.name }}" | available: {{ e.available }} | quantity: {{ e.quantity }}
{% endfor %}configured locations:
{% for line in config_lines %}  - "{{ line | split: '|' | first | strip }}"
{% endfor %}</pre>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
